  "summary_text": "Kyle, yesterday was flat at Port Washington and a retail-only day at Hicksville, both predictable ahead of Columbus Day headwinds today. The real story is year-to-date momentum and a specific productivity signal you should own.\n\nPort Washington delivered $30.5K MTD against a DOW-adjusted expectation of $32.1K\u2014that's a real 5% performance gap, not calendar noise. The gap is operational: add-on attach collapsed to 60% from 78% last week, signaling softer upsell discipline, while retail also underperformed (down 7%). Grooming core revenue stayed solid (+3%), so the team's executing appointments, but they're not maximizing the ticket. Hicksville is outpacing its DOW-adjusted forecast (+1.2%) and MTD is up 8% year-over-year\u2014that location is punching above weight. Be proud of this: year-to-date you're up 38% in revenue and 37% in appointments across the established footprint, a genuinely strong trajectory. Glen Cove is still establishing retail baseline and has zero grooming scheduled next week\u2014clarify the intent there.\n\nThe pattern across both active locations: groomer-days are down slightly MTD (48 at Port, 28 at Hicksville vs. prior month), and productivity per groomer is below trailing-30-day baseline at Port Washington ($451 vs. $503). Hicksville's $/groomer-day is up ($446 vs. $382), but that's off a smaller prior base. Capacity is tightening at Port\u2014your larger revenue driver\u2014and you need more groomer-days or higher attach to close the MTD gap.\n\nPort Washington: 5 groomers, 15.0h bathers today; 6 groomers, 0.0h bathers tomorrow; 35 groomer-days next 7 days. Hicksville: 1 groomer, 0.0h bathers today; 3 groomers, 0.0h bathers tomorrow; 22 groomer-days next 7 days."
